Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by incorrect accesses to the `planes` member of the `vb2_v4l2_buffer` structure instead of the intended `vb2_buffer` structure. This occurred after a previous commit changed the return types of buffer helper functions but did not update all relevant accesses to the `planes` member, leading to values being read from and written to the wrong memory locations.

Here is the patch:

 static void vb2ops_venc_stop_streaming(struct vb2_queue *q)
 {
